The $x$-coordinate $p$ of the vertex of the parabola $y=ax^2+c$ is given by the formula $p=\frac{-b}{2a}$.  For a parabola in the form $y=ax^2+bx+c$, the $a$-, $b$- and $c$-values are 1, 6, and $-7$.  Plugging into the formula yields $p=\frac{-6}{2(1)}=-3$ so the vertex of this parabola lies on the line $a=-3$.  Plugging this value into the given equation yields the minimum value of the quadratic as $a = (-3)^2+6(-3)-7 = \boxed{-22}$. </think> <answer> -22 </answer>

